## Package *brms* makes it easy for us

Despite the complexities of how this works under the hood, *brms* will make it feel familiar




::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
library(brms)

x <- runif(100, 0, 1)
mu <- exp(-2 + 4 * x)
y <- rpois(length(x), mu)
dat <- data.frame(x, y)

m <- brm(y ~ x, data = dat, 
         family = poisson(), 
         prior = c(prior(normal(0, 1000), class = Intercept),
                   prior(normal(0, 1000), class = b)))
```
:::


## Package *brms* makes it easy for us

Despite the complexities of how this works under the hood, *brms* will make it feel familiar


